":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["20\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Taris sees an economic boom in the years leading up to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Great Sith War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Great_Sith_War"},", thanks in part to the support of speeder manufacturer ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lhosan Industries"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lhosan_Industries","referenceId":"reference:243f88645fb81a36"},". During ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Mandalorian Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Mandalorian_Wars"},", Lhosan withdraws its support from Taris, and the planet's prosperity decays rapidly.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["25\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Like other city-planets, Taris is divided into multiple city layers, as well as districts. Inhabitants of the Upper City maintain a luxurious lifestyle, but those in the Lower City and the Undercity live without comforts.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["30\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["The Undercity of Taris is infested with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rakghouls"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rakghouls"},", a species of mutated, feral humanoids, who plague the planet's less fortunate inhabitants.\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
